### Names and descriptions of features added with fields (toolbar)
### The ID is the feature type without its version (@1), with "." and "_" turned into "-", prefixed by feature-. Descriptions add -tip.

feature-solid-hole = Hole
feature-solid-hole-tip = Drill a hole at every lone sketch point (points not used by lines or circles)
feature-solid-shell = Shell
feature-solid-shell-tip = Hollow out a solid into a shell. Selected faces are removed to open it; selecting a body makes a closed cavity inside
feature-solid-boolean = Combine
feature-solid-boolean-tip = Join, cut or intersect tool bodies with the target body (any number of tools)
feature-solid-split = Split Body
feature-solid-split-tip = Split a body in two with a plane (to cut the top and bottom in separate setups, for example). The side the normal points to keeps the original body's name; the other side becomes a new body
feature-solid-move = Move/Copy
feature-solid-move-tip = Move or rotate bodies by value (with Copy on, the original is kept). Nothing moves until a value is entered
feature-solid-delete-faces = Delete Faces
feature-solid-delete-faces-tip = Delete the selected faces and extend the surrounding faces to close the gap (deleting fillet or chamfer faces brings back the corner)
feature-solid-draft = Draft
feature-solid-draft-tip = Tilt the selected flat faces about their intersection with the pull-direction plane (a draft for releasing from a mold). Surrounding faces extend or shrink
feature-solid-offset-faces = Offset Faces
feature-solid-offset-faces-tip = Move the selected faces along their normals. Positive adds material, negative removes it (works on curved faces too; a negative value on a hole wall widens the hole)
feature-solid-replace-face = Replace Face
feature-solid-replace-face-tip = Replace the selected flat faces (source faces) with the plane of the target face. Surrounding faces extend or shrink
feature-solid-scale = Scale
feature-solid-scale-tip = Resize bodies by a factor about a base point (non-uniform scales X, Y and Z separately)
feature-cad-datum-axis = Construction Axis
feature-cad-datum-axis-tip = Create a straight line to use as an axis for revolves and patterns (through two points, along an edge, a cylinder's axis, or where two planes meet)
feature-cad-datum-plane = Construction Plane
feature-cad-datum-plane-tip = Create a plane to use as a reference for sketches and features (offset from a face or plane, tilted about an axis, midway between two faces, or through three points)
feature-cad-datum-point = Construction Point
feature-cad-datum-point-tip = Create a point to use as a reference for construction planes and axes (a body corner, the center of a circular edge, or coordinates)
feature-solid-mirror = Mirror
feature-solid-mirror-tip = Copy a feature's shape to the other side of a plane (joined for a new-body feature, cut for a cut)
feature-solid-linear-pattern = Rectangular Pattern
feature-solid-linear-pattern-tip = Repeat a feature's shape at a constant spacing
feature-solid-circular-pattern = Circular Pattern
feature-solid-circular-pattern-tip = Repeat a feature's shape around an axis
feature-fea-static = Static Stress
feature-fea-static-tip = Add fixed faces and loads to see stress, displacement and safety factor in color (a linear, small-deformation estimate)
feature-fea-thermal = Thermal
feature-fea-thermal-tip = Add faces with set temperatures, faces where heat comes in and faces losing heat to the air to see steady-state or time-varying temperature distributions in color
feature-fea-modal = Modal Frequencies
feature-fea-modal-tip = Add fixed faces to see the frequencies it vibrates at easily (resonance) and the mode shapes. Compare them with the spindle speed (about 170–400 Hz)
feature-fea-topology = Lightweight Shape Guide
feature-fea-topology-tip = From fixtures and loads, see a reference shape that keeps only what is needed to carry the forces (the shape is unchanged; look at it and sketch the pockets yourself)
feature-flow-wing = Wing Lift
feature-flow-wing-tip = Find lift, induced drag and neutral point of wing bodies (main wing, tail) with the vortex lattice method (up is +Z)
feature-flow-section = 2D Flow
feature-flow-section-tip = Cut a body with a section to see the surrounding flow (speed, pressure, vorticity) and drag (lattice Boltzmann method)
feature-flow-volume = 3D Flow
feature-flow-volume-tip = Solve the 3D flow and drag around a body to see surface pressure and streamlines, and speed, pressure and vorticity on a section (takes about a minute)
